WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.170
- Like a lot of people,

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:02.160
you dealt with stagefright.

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:03.038
I didn't know that in the beginning.

00:00:03.038 --> 00:00:04.229
- Oh yeah.
- I had no idea.

00:00:04.229 --> 00:00:05.280
- You don't have any stagefright.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:06.810
I know. You're very, you're like-

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.130
- It's not that I'm...

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:09.090
It's not that I'm...

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:10.710
I mean, I'm a fair amount of confident.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.790
I just mean like we're probably

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:13.260
gonna screw up though sometimes.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:14.160
So like, whatever.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:14.993
- You can't be perfect.

00:00:14.993 --> 00:00:16.290
I know.
- Yeah. I think I just have

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:18.325
such a low bar expectation wise.

00:00:18.325 --> 00:00:20.190
(audience laughs)
I'm like, I mean,

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:21.840
I'm gonna do my best.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.480
And I feel like sometimes it happens,

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:25.927
and you have nights where you're like,

00:00:25.927 --> 00:00:26.820
"I did amazing."

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:27.653
And you have nights where you're like,

00:00:27.653 --> 00:00:29.221
"Why am I-
- Yeah. Why-

00:00:29.221 --> 00:00:30.603
- Why did people pay for this?

00:00:30.603 --> 00:00:32.176
- (Shania laughs) "Why
do people pay for this?"

00:00:32.176 --> 00:00:33.737
- (Kelly laughs) Yeah.
- No. I think my-

00:00:33.737 --> 00:00:35.220
- How did you get over that?

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.270
- Well it started more just because

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:38.250
I was singing in bars from
the age of eight years old.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.780
Very intimidating environment.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.250
And everybody's already drunk,

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.840
and they're falling everywhere.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.250
- [Kelly] At eight?
- Yeah.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.290
Cigarettes, you know, it just wasn't...

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:47.867
And I think it was more...

00:00:47.867 --> 00:00:49.408
(Shania bursts into
laughter) Yes, that's me.

00:00:49.408 --> 00:00:51.540
- Little bitty. Little bitty Shania.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:55.470
- In bars. And so I think
I learned very young

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:57.607
to put on a front, a mask of like,

00:00:57.607 --> 00:01:00.090
"Okay, you know, I'm up
here and I'm professional."

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:01.170
- Yeah.
- And you know,

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:03.450
and, but I was petrified.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:04.530
I was so uncomfortable.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.453
And I think it just stayed with me.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.170
Never really finding my
comfort zone out there

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.490
for a long, long time.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.410
I'm in a way better place now.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:14.340
I don't know what happened.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.450
I think many things happened,

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.583
but I grew up, I guess.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:21.120
But very recently I'm much
more comfortable with it now.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.010
I just see things differently.

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:24.450
- Yeah.
- But whoa. No, no.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.220
For many, many, many, many years

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:27.600
till like I said, very recently,

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:28.890
it was always very (indistinct).

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:29.850
- I always feel sorry.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:32.850
I know a lot, a lot of artists
actually struggle with that.

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:34.440
And I'm like,

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.170
I don't know if I'd go
out on stage and do it.

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:38.460
I think that you're brave.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:39.450
If I ever felt like that,

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:41.850
I don't think I would follow through.

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:42.810
- It's torture.

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:44.310
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- It really is torture

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:45.330
to have that anxiety.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:46.380
- And when I get nervous,

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:47.730
my stomach does this thing

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:48.870
where-
- Yeah. What happens,

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:49.703
do you get cramps?
- Well it's kind of like

00:01:49.703 --> 00:01:50.907
a bridesmaid scenario.

00:01:50.907 --> 00:01:51.914
(Kelly and the audience laugh)

00:01:51.914 --> 00:01:53.797
It's like, you know, you're like,

00:01:53.797 --> 00:01:55.830
"Oh my gosh, is this
gonna happen on stage?"

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:57.784
Like your horse.
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.520
I get, I'm just saying,

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.290
my stomach, when I get really nervous,

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:02.355
that's what happens.
- Uh-oh.

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:04.980
- Like my stomach just turns.
- That kicks in? Uh-oh.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:06.510
- Yeah. So what am I gonna do?

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:07.343
Yeah. No.

00:02:07.343 --> 00:02:08.940
- I mean a lot of people do,

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:10.613
you know, vomit before they go on stage.

00:02:10.613 --> 00:02:13.410
- I know.
- And I know, it's a reaction.

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:14.940
But I did learn from a very young age,

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:15.930
the mind over matter.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:17.097
You know, put the mask on-
- Yeah.

00:02:17.097 --> 00:02:19.380
- Get out there, and nobody should see

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:22.140
that you're, what you're really feeling.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:25.020
So I was, I got good at that very young,

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:27.930
and managed it, but, oh, oh, oh no.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.100
Very scary feeling.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.210
- I'm glad that you don't get it now,

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:31.350
'cause you're so awesome live.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:32.820
I think that's what's
so awesome about you,

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.440
is you're very welcoming.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:35.910
You know what I'm saying,
even if you're not right-

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:38.460
- Talk about miss welcoming herself.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.440
- No. I think that that's very,

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.300
that's what is so captivating.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.740
You're like, even if you do mess up,

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:45.330
it's like whatever, everybody messes up.

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.010
I messed up like 10 times today already.

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:49.140
Like, it happens, it's fine.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:50.530
- You have to be okay with that.

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:52.320
- Yeah.
- It's kind of like, you know,

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:54.930
the people that learn
a language more quickly

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:57.000
are the ones that are not
afraid to make mistakes

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:57.833
as they're learning it.

00:02:57.833 --> 00:03:00.180
Otherwise, you never, you
never practice it out loud.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:02.295
You never, you know, put it,

00:03:02.295 --> 00:03:03.471
- Not afraid to look stupid or something.

00:03:03.471 --> 00:03:04.304
- You're not afraid to look stupid.

00:03:04.304 --> 00:03:06.240
- You have to be, you
have to really be ready.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:07.770
And listen, on stage,

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:09.630
if you hit the wrong note,
you forget the words,

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:11.130
you do look stupid,

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:14.100
but your fans are there
because they love you,

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.296
and it's a mutual respect
thing so it's fine.

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:17.220
- Even if it's not every night,

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:18.300
it just happens every once in a while.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.890
That's why I guess I
don't, I don't get it.

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:23.970
'Cause I'm like, I'm bound
to suck a lot sometimes.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.020
It's gonna happen, so.

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:25.980
- You do not.

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:27.690
You are so great live.

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:29.730
You're amazing. You're just one of these

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:32.115
such incredible singers of our time.

00:03:32.115 --> 00:03:32.948
(audience applauds)

00:03:32.948 --> 00:03:34.010
- Oh, you're, you're very nice.

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:35.963
- I honestly though,

00:03:35.963 --> 00:03:37.650
I think that's why I like
listening to you too,

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.570
is like, it's just
listening to the artists

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:41.610
that like, you're not doing
it 'cause you have to,

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:43.050
you're doing it 'cause you love it,

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:44.460
and there's a difference, you know.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:46.080
You're not doing it as
'cause it's just a job.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.730
You sound like you love what you do,

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:48.563
and you're all in.

00:03:48.563 --> 00:03:50.180
Like your whole body. I love that.

